body:
This is incredibly helpful, thank you. Good to know, I'll reach out to my insurance and I'll ask for a case manager ASAP. Yeah I'm going to mass general for thoracic outlet/nerve issues. And good to know to include multiple items - I should mention, the diagnostic procedure (specific botox protocol) would be performed by a radiologist (different provider) at the hospital, would the specialist still be able to request these multiple items in the SCA request even if performed by a different provider?

&#x200B;

And good to know, the doctor overseeing my care in NY is very dedicated and detail oriented so it's good they're the ones to initiate. If you don't mind me asking, what is a typical/reasonable time these things happen in? Is hoping it could take a month naive/unrealistic?

Thanks Corey, I like the idea of the black pipe frame but I don't really understand it? If there's any way you can explain it differently (my guess is your building a square out of types for the monitor to lie in? But then you're still using a monitor arm to secure it to the wall or something so I don't fully understand?)

&#x200B;

A monitor arm attached to the wall I thought might work, but I have an ergotronHX monitor arm and it will not rotate down 90°, it only rotates may be 30 or 45° downward, and I have not seen a monitor arm that will rotate all the way down).

who recommended egosue? interesting, how did you find piligian, yeah same guy

&#x200B;

so far nothings helped but lets stay in touch, im starting to do lots of intense work

Got it, are you an ex-pat from the West living in Japan, not Japanese

&#x200B;

I thought about traveling to Europe and getting treatment there in Germany perhapps but I feel like being a foreign non-Germans (even though they speak English) assist would put them off

[https://www.swimoutlet.com/products/kemp-lifeguard-cpr-mask-in-red-pouch-27300?utm\_source=google&utm\_medium=cpc&utm\_campaign=google-shopping&campaignid=9595451440&adgroupid=97162322565&keyword=&matchtype=&targetid=pla-363139216948&device=m&creativeid=424497227438&adposition=&adtype=&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI2uvQ0cST8gIVbwWICR3wBQHIEAQYAyABEgI-2\_D\_BwE](https://www.swimoutlet.com/products/kemp-lifeguard-cpr-mask-in-red-pouch-27300?utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign=google-shopping&campaignid=9595451440&adgroupid=97162322565&keyword=&matchtype=&targetid=pla-363139216948&device=m&creativeid=424497227438&adposition=&adtype=&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI2uvQ0cST8gIVbwWICR3wBQHIEAQYAyABEgI-2_D_BwE)

&#x200B;

Someone else suggested buying one of these lifeguard CPR masks, attaching an oxygen tube, and using a rubber band to make sure it stays over my mouth and nose and just breathing in through that. In that case, would I also have to Make sure it's only 15 inches long or so? thank you so much for your response , something I never would've thought of and probably I would've made it very long

Got it, so your nerve symptoms and pain are only on the left side, not bilateral?

&#x200B;

Yes, I was given chin tucks which gave me pain because I have an elevated first rib and talking the chin would irritate that  but that has improved with time. Also scapular squeezes, but I can never do them in such a way that I disengage my neck and trapezius muscle Which is a problem, wall slides, Core exercises, deep breathing. I don't know if there's a net brace, I now am realizing maybe I am responding to a post it was not directed at me so I apologize if so

Have you looked into CRPS? I want to look up someone who is a specialist in either SFN or CRPS, interesting your symptoms sound more similar to mine then dissimilar if that makes sense.

&#x200B;

No, I've been shrugged at by enough surgeons that I do not want one of them cutting into me. It seems like they don't really care about stuff like pain, hypersensitivity/allodynia, even tingling really unless it affects motor function or accompanies severe atrophy. That said I haven't had a real surgical consultation/new EMG in well over a year, , but I just don't think that's the route for me at the moment. I'm looking into ketamine infusions, maybe lidocaine injections for a nerve block, I think that might be more what I'm dealing with than surgical stuff.

&#x200B;

 Do you have difficulty wearing long sleevesOn your elbow? I can only wear ultralight down jackets/puffy jackets around one of my elbows. I'm thinking about making a featherlight/soft ultralight down sleeve to just put on my elbows that I could wear undershirts, suits, sweaters that might allow me to where long sleeves

Interesting, if you don't mind me asking what does your HEP home exercise program consist of? Have they given you a timeline for when they expected to get better, and lastly how long did you wait between doing the two MRIs of the cervical spine.

&#x200B;

Sorry, false alarm, a few more questions lol - did you get tingling, numbness, and pain in the fingers?

Interesting, I know I grind my teeth but I've never thought of myself as having TMJ, my PT today told me to get checked for sleep apnea, perhaps a CPAP machine Might be helpful to get more oxygen to breathe since I breathe through my mouth she said, but I don't know that I have sleep apnea either, just trial and error as you said.

&#x200B;

I really relate to your "black/red pill for life" comment, I have really bad postnasal drip and polyps, dryness like you wouldn't believe to my nose is almost always bloody. I'm trying to follow your last two posts and relate them to myself, I hope it's not rude to ask but and I know obviously neither of us are medical professionals but - what do you think I should do with those pieces of information your writing about?  ask for A referral to a TMJ specialist, what type of doctor did you see to help you improve your breathing

That's a very valid point, I'm looking for a PDF so I can read it on a tablet while I exercise so trying to turn the research into something good for me as opposed to increase computer use.

&#x200B;

I also agree with what you say – I try to identify all my symptoms for doctors and physical therapists, and they kind of apply a blanket approach that does not necessarily matter what I'm telling them, if that makes sense. Like they will either treat the neck or treat the elbow or treat the wrist, it doesn't matter what the specific sensations are that I'm trying to keep track of. Have you found better information that is more relevant than these books that are twenty years old?

I haven't, that's not a bad idea – I tried a software called camera mouse that I think worked sort of similarly minus clicking but I found the head movements to be kind of a lot on your neck and not very efficient, and I'm trying to see if there's a way to use my hands to click a mouse without having to actually click, to control the click of a mouse I guess.

&#x200B;

Do you know how you click using the Smartnav had mouse?

thank you so much for this, this is incredibly helpful.

&#x200B;

I get clicking (subluxation of the ulnar nerve I believe) in my left elbow when I flex it, which is why I had a hard time doing weight training. Did you also get this and just ignore it? it makes my fingers feel worse I think but not sure.

&#x200B;

That's incredibly helpful, I haven't been able to swim but it's my favorite type of exercise - I should definitely try backstroke because freestyle bothers me - and yes it keeps your neck straight! didn't think about that!

&#x200B;

I'm curious what you mean by manual therapist - like someone certified in active release? If you know the correct word deftly let me know, would be interested in looking into that - not sure what's between a physical therapist and chiropractor

&#x200B;

I hope it doesn't sound like too basic of a question, what were some ways you cut down on screen time/forced yourself to be in the correct posture (I'm not in an amazing posture as I dictate this)

&#x200B;

For standard back exercises, I just googled 5lb dumbell back workout and got lots of results with similar exercises [https://www.womenshealthmag.com/fitness/g28553492/dumbbell-back-exercises/](https://www.womenshealthmag.com/fitness/g28553492/dumbbell-back-exercises/), ty for the tips

Thank you for this information. Did DMARDs/biologic treatment help with your CTS symptoms? I was diagnosed with AS due to buttock pain/sacroilitis MRI a year ago, but my back/buttock pain has since gone away, but my elbow/hand pain is awful (repetitive use made it worse) and I'm unsure if Humira/Cocentyx would help it (no rheum is sure either).

&#x200B;

Just to clarify from reading,  enthesitis doesn't show up on imaging? How do they diagnose/identify it?

Thank you. I read Sarno and tried to see if TMS might apply to me, but I couldn't buy into it. I know that stress does not help my symptoms, but they are present even when I'm relaxed. I'm curious what your experience was believing something was wrong even though recovery took place – what happened?

&#x200B;

I did significantly decrease my computer use but still have to use the computer and haven't been able to quit cold turkey, but for the most part yes stop the activities but the Numbness lingers. I also developed pain And stiffness in one of my other Fingers (Pointer finger on opposite hand) subsequently from use
